Measured on synapse 2026-11-19 04:56 UTC (cai-fleet): /var/log/skeid/events/ holds one file per usage event, ~28k files / 113 MB after five days of light traffic; 'ls events/*' fails with 'Argument list too long'. Disk is fine (11 %), but the directory grows without bound. Decide: daily files or rotation, and let usage_store.retention_days / skeid usage-purge --retention cover the jsonlog store with a schedule (Changes says both built-in stores purge — check that jsonlog honours it in this layout). Test with a directory of many files.

2026-11-25 05:33 Layout: dir mode writes <path>/YYYY-MM-DD/<id>.json, the UTC day of the id's time (= write time; created_at may be caller-supplied, e.g. backfilled). Day dir cached per store object (_ready_day): one mkdir per day, EEXIST ok; sysopen ENOENT (a purge removed the dir) clears the cache and retries. report/purge list via readdir (not glob) over day dirs + legacy flat *.json, sorted by id. Purge rmdirs a day dir it leaves without events; ENOTEMPTY/EEXIST/ENOENT ignored, other errors fail the purge (repeatable). New t/99-usage-jsonlog-day-dirs.t red (events landed flat) then green, 49 tests incl. 5000-file case (~1s). Updated layout assertions in t/16, t/18, t/52 (collision seed pinned into a day dir), t/68, t/69, t/88 (read events from day dirs).

